window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["audi/a1-8x"]={"a1-8x-facelift-activate-dvd-playback-while-driving-vim":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_facelift-13095418.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to remove the MMI protection and continue watching a DVD or video while driving (Video in Motion).   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Step 1: Recovering the MMI 3GP serial number</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Advanced Ident -1A</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Retrieve serial number (if more than one, use the <strong>first</strong> one!)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_mmi_plus_5f_seriennummer-PNG-12291981.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Calculating the security code</strong></p>\n<p>Enter the serial number previously retrieved from the website (your choice, subject to availability):  </p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.audienthusiasts.com/Articles_VIM.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AUDIENTHUSIATS VIM</a></p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.bestcarmods.com/vim/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">BESTCARMODS VIM</a></p>\n<p>The site will display your security code.<br/><em>An alternative security code is also generated.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 3: Enter security code</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Secure access -16</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Enter security code <br/><em>(Use alternative security code if first code does not work)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 4: Removing the protection</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation -10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>48</strong> </p>\n<p><em>Set value to <strong>255</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 5: Restart the MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press MENU + Wheel + Top right button</p>","a1-8x-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-cd-dvd-extraction":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A1 8X facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_facelift-13095418.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates CD/DVD extraction in the DVD player. Allows you to import / copy all CD/DVD / SD card content to the MMI 3G PLUS jukebox (hard disk).   </p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) :</em> <a href=\"#/audi/a1-8x/a1-8x-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-hidden-menu\">Activate MMI 3GP hidden menu</a></em></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; import_multimedia -&gt; Tick <strong>Ripping</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi3g_plus_hidden_menu_cd-ripping-cbf13d3b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p><em>Press MENU + Wheel + Top Right button.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/import_ripping_mmi3g_vagcoding-af2ca0fd.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-hidden-menu":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_facelift-13095418.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the hidden green menu (green menu, hidden menu, test mode, engineer mode) in the Audi MMI 3G PLUS. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“5F – Electrical Information.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 6</strong> </em>and set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>No need to restart the MMI.</em></p>\n<p><em><em>To open the Hidden Menu, press MENU + CAR (simultaneously for 6 seconds), or press the CAR button first.</em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/a7_mmi_plus-bb5ba729.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_navigation_plus_mmi3g_hidden_menue-ae4ebd5e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> select the “Bootloader” option!</p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/access-the-audi-red-engineering-menu\">–&gt; To access the Audi Red Engineering menu</a></strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"#/t/enabling-the-hidden-menu-for-audi-mmi-3g-and-3g\"><strong>–&gt; Enable the hidden MMI 3G/3G+ menu without VCDS or OBDeleven</strong></a></p>","a1-8x-facelift-bluetooth-mmi-3gp-activation":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_facelift-13095418.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth with an Audi MMI 3G PLUS.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"#/audi/a1-8x/a1-8x-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-hidden-menu\">Activate MMI 3GP Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Activate Bluetooth in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + MENU</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>diagnostics  &gt;  settings  &gt;  tel_settings -&gt;  Select <strong>“HFP activation”</strong><br/>diagnose   &gt;  settings  &gt;  tel_settings -&gt;  Select <strong>“BT activation”</strong><br/>diagnostics   &gt;  settings  &gt;  tel_settings -&gt;  Select  <strong>“BT defaut visibility” to [auto] 1/3</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_tel_settings-af0d9718.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; ami_aux -&gt; Select <strong>AMI BT [enabled] 1/2</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ami_bt-8fa46d9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p><em>Press MENU + Wheel + Top Right button.</em></p>\n<p><br/><strong>Step 3: Bluetooth activation with VCDS</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong> and then click on ” “.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 17</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Module_5F_Adaptation_Channel17-d3fc3a63.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-facelift-change-mmi-3gp-start-logo":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_facelift-13095418.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the Splash Screen of the MMI 3G PLUS.  </p>\n<p><em>For a custom logo see tuto: A1 (8X) Facelift – MMI 3G/3GP custom start logo</em></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"#/audi/a1-8x/a1-8x-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-hidden-menu\">Activate MMI 3GP Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Change the start logo in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>car -&gt; carcodingvehicle -&gt; Select No Of Screen</p>\n<p><em>Select the desired display:</em><br/><em><br/>0 -&gt;  Standard display<br/>1 -&gt;  Standard display<br/>2 -&gt;  A8<br/>3 -&gt;  S8<br/>4 -&gt;  W12<br/>5 -&gt;  A6<br/>6 -&gt;  S6<br/>7 -&gt;  RS6<br/>8 -&gt;  A6 allroad<br/>9 -&gt;  A7<br/>10 -&gt;  S7<br/>11 -&gt;  RS7<br/>12 -&gt;  A1<br/>13 -&gt;  S1<br/>14 -&gt;  Q3<br/>15 -&gt;  A4<br/>16 -&gt;  A4 allroad<br/>17 -&gt;  S4<br/>18 -&gt;  RS4<br/>19 -&gt;  A5<br/>20 -&gt;  S5<br/>21 -&gt;  RS5<br/>22 -&gt;  Q5<br/>23 -&gt;  Q5 Hybrid<br/>24 -&gt;  Q7<br/>25 -&gt;  Q7 Hybrid<br/>26 -&gt;  SQ5<br/>27 -&gt;  Standard display<br/>28 -&gt;  Standard display<br/>29 -&gt;  Standard display</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/splashscreenmmi3gp-6fcb5f6a.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S1-8fca826d.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-facelift-enable-bluetooth-streaming-audio-a2dp-mmi-3gp":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_facelift-13095418.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables Bluetooth streaming audio on the MMI 3G PLUS, so you can listen to music from your A2DP-compatible audio player.  </p>\n<p><em>ATTENTION: You must have activated the Hidden Menu (<a href=\"#/audi/a1-8x/a1-8x-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-hidden-menu\">Activate hidden menu MMI 3GP</a>)</em> and enabled Bluetooth (either by default or via the “Activate Bluetooth MMI 3GP” tutorial).  </p>\n<p>Press CAR + MENU (for 6s)</p>\n<p>diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; ami_aux -&gt; Select <strong>AMI BT [enabled] 1/2</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ami_bt-8fa46d9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>bluetooth -&gt; Check <strong>A2DP Activation</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ad2p-90e760bc.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Restart MMI</p>\n<p><em>Press MENU + Wheel + Top Right button.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ad2p_v2-660aabbb.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ad2p_v3-6ac58876.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-facelift-activate-hill-start-assist":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_facelift-13095418.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables Audi Hill Start Assist.  </p>\n<p>Audi Hill Start Assist is a hill-start assist feature. If you hold down the brake pedal for a certain amount of time while the vehicle is stopped, brake pressure is maintained for a few seconds after you release the brake pedal, making it easier to start on a hill.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong><strong>Brakes </strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>” then<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>22</strong>: </em> <br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check the </em>box</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong><strong>Brakes </strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Hill Start Assistant</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6 – </strong> On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the value based on your preference:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>“<strong>normal</strong>” (default value)</li>\n<li>“<strong>Early</strong>” (faster trigger)</li>\n<li>“<strong>Late</strong>” (later trigger)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>then click “Submit.”</p>","a1-8x-facelift-mmi-3g-3gp-customized-start-logo":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_facelift-13095418.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To modify and/or customize the home screen logo (Custom Splash Screen) with a personalized image of the MMI 3G and 3GPLUS. <br/><br/>Start by downloading the script file: <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/download/MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen_VAG-Coding.fr.zip\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen_VAG-Coding.en.zip</a></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed </strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Then extract the file you just downloaded: MMI 3G 3GP SplashScreen VAG-Coding.en.zip</li>\n<li>Go to the “splashscreens” folder and edit the “startup_generic.png” image if you wish. You can edit this image, modify it or import another image, to have your own startup logo (keep the same PNG format and image size 800×480) or an image found in the “samples” folder (copy it into the “splashscreens” folder with the name startup_generic.png. </li>\n<li>Copy the contents of the MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen folder to a FAT32-formatted SD card (max. 32GB).</li>\n<li>Start your AUDI and let the MMI boot up, it takes a few seconds.</li>\n<li>Disconnect your smartphone’s Bluetooth if there’s a link between it and the MMI, and remove all your SD cards (SD1 &amp; SD2)…</li>\n<li>Then insert the SD card you have prepared into slot SD1.</li>\n<li>You’ll see green text asking you to turn the large knob on your MMI central console, and the message will disappear.</li>\n<li>Wait a few moments. A new message will appear stating that all has gone well and that your image has been imported successfully. </li>\n<li>Restart the MMI using the button combination that corresponds to your AUDI.<br/>Example: Press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right button (3) at the same time.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>If your new start-up screen does not appear when your MMI reboots, go to the green hidden menu<em> (to activate the hidden menu, follow the “Activate MMI 3G or 3GP hidden menu” tutorial).</em></p>\n<p>For <strong>MMI 3GP </strong>: Select in <strong>car </strong>-&gt;<strong> carcodingvehicle </strong>-&gt;<strong> Select n° screen </strong>-&gt;<strong> set cursor to 0</strong>, then restart your MMI.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/splashscreenmmi3gp-6fcb5f6a.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>For <strong>MMI 3G</strong>: <strong>car</strong> -&gt; <strong>carcodingvehicle</strong> -&gt; <strong>configuration line</strong> -&gt; <em><strong>[standard] 2/5</strong> (Standard home screen)</em> then restart your MMI.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6876-ad94c126.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Your very own Splash Screen will appear!<br/>Many images are available in the zip file… both the original and modified ones.</p>\n<p><em>A problem?  </em>If the script doesn’t run the first time, try again. You’ve only copied the contents of the MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen folder? Do not copy the folder, just its contents!  <br/>For MMI 3G Basic: If your image does not appear or is truncated, resize the image to 400 by 240.</p>\n<hr/>\n<ul><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A1-cca1d214.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A1-quattro-d5c05d6b.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-ec35ba13.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-allroad-ecfb784b.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-Hybrid-8b3bc272.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6L-da4efe88.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A7-0413e2db.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A8-b82aa2e7.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A8-Hybrid-bf48c947.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Q3-f5806bdd.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Q5-137fb9fc.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RS6-99c35be3.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RS7-973708ca.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RSQ3-82016453.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RSQ5-4b2a2aa7.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S1-8fca826d.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-ff017200.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-png_APR-b51955a9.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-APR-5b67cc13.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S7-1b8e075e.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S8-1a7397d6.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Vierge-e6bcc4e4.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_W12-9cbddbdf.webp\"/></figure></li></ul><a></a><a></a><a></a>","a1-8x-activate-dvd-playback-while-driving-vim":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Allows you to remove the MMI protection and continue watching a DVD or video while driving (Video in Motion).   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Step 1: Retrieving the MMI 2G/3G serial number</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>“for <strong>MMI 3G</strong> or<strong>“07 – Display/Cmde</strong>” for <strong>MMI 2G</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Advanced Ident -1A</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Retrieve serial number (if more than one, use the <strong>first</strong> one!)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_mmi_plus_5f_seriennummer-PNG-12291981.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Calculating the security code</strong></p>\n<p>Enter the serial number previously retrieved from the website (your choice, subject to availability):  </p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.audienthusiasts.com/Articles_VIM.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AUDIENTHUSIATS VIM</a></p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.bestcarmods.com/vim/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">BESTCARMODS VIM</a></p>\n<p>The site will display your security code.<br/><em>An alternative security code is also generated.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 3: Enter security code</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>“for <strong>MMI 3G</strong> or<strong>“07 – Display/Cmde</strong>” for <strong>MMI 2G</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Secure access -16</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Enter security code <br/><em>(Use alternative security code if first code does not work)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 4: Removing the protection</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>“for <strong>MMI 3G</strong> or<strong>“07 – Display/Cmde</strong>” for <strong>MMI 2G</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation -10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>48</strong> for <strong>MMI 3G</strong> or Channel <strong>63</strong> for <strong>MMI 2G</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to <strong>255</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 5: Restart the MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press MENU + Wheel + Top right button</p>","a1-8x-activate-mmi-rmc-hidden-menu":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the hidden green menu (green menu, hidden menu, test mode, engineer mode) in the Audi MMI RMC.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>5F – Electrical Information</strong></strong>” / <strong>“56 – Radio”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 5</strong> </em>and set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em><em>No need to restart the MMI.</em></em></p>\n<p><em>To open the Hidden Menu, press MENU + CAR (for 6 seconds)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g-217db9e1.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/access-the-audi-red-engineering-menu\">–&gt; To access the Audi Red Engineering menu</a></strong></p>","a1-8x-activate-rearview-camera-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To activate the reversing camera after it has been installed on the MMI RMC or 3GP. <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>“.<br/><br/> 4 – Select <strong>“Installation List”</strong><br/><br/> 5 – Tick:<strong>“6C – Rear View Camera</strong>” in the list</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Save coding</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“6C – Rear view camera</strong>“.<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/> 5 – <strong>Coding</strong>:  </p>\n<p>1030015 = Automatic hitch, with APS+.</p>\n<p>1000015 = RVC only</p>\n<p>1020015 = APS+, without automatic coupler</p>\n<p>1010015 = Automatic hitch, without APS+.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/>For MMI RMC :<br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte <strong>6</strong><br/>Then set bit <strong>2</strong></p>\n<p>For MMI 3GP: <br/> 6 – Select byte <strong>7</strong><br/>Then set bit <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Hardware upgrade :</strong></p>\n<p>The camera’s video cable is connected to the infotainment control unit. It is installed in the glovebox.   </p>\n<p><br/>The 2 pins of the reversing camera are used in the 12-pin quadlock (blue). Usable cable set: Part no. 000 979 009 E <br/><br/>Quadblock Assignment :<br/><br/>Pin 5 = video line<br/>Pin 11 = shielding</p>","a1-8x-aps-radar-volume":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to select the volume of the Audi Parking System radars.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 (Rear radar volume) :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>10 – Assistance stationn</strong>”.  <br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p>5 – Select<em>“Speaker volume for rear park assist</em>” from the value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Choose the new value from the second list (from Stage 1 to Stage 9)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Front Radar Volume):</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click <strong>“10 – Parking Assist”</strong> <br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p>5 – Select<em>“Speaker volume for front park assist</em>” from the value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Choose the new value from the second list (from Stage 1 to Stage 9)</p>","a1-8x-audi-parking-system-deactivation-speed":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to select the deactivation speed of the Audi Parking System.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>10 – Assistance stationn</strong>”.  <br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p>5 – Select<em>“Switch-off speed for parking assist</em>” from the value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Choose a value between <strong>0 and 20 km/h</strong></p>","a1-8x-automatic-folding-of-mirrors":"<p><strong>Function:</strong> Automatically folds the side mirrors when the vehicle is locked. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“42 – Driver’s Door.”</strong></p>\n<p>4 – Click on “Coding – 07” then “Long Coding Helper”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>04</strong>: </em><br/>Check Bit <strong>6</strong> <em><em>(If it is a hidden bit, you must modify the binary value directly (replace the 0 with a 1, e.g.,<strong>01011100</strong>)).</em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mirrors-d6746b16.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“52 – Passenger Door.”</strong></p>\n<p>4 – Click on “Coding – 07” then “Long Coding Helper”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>04</strong>: </em><br/><em>.</em> Set Bit <strong>6</strong> <em>(If it is a hidden bit, you must modify the binary value directly (replace the 0 with a 1, e.g.,<strong>01011100</strong>)).</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mirrors-d6746b16.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong><em>Notes:</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>The side mirrors will extend automatically when the ignition is turned on.</em></li>\n<li><em>The side mirrors will fold in automatically when you lock the vehicle with the remote control.</em></li>\n<li><em>To automatically fold the side mirrors using the Audi Advanced Key, you must press and hold the button on the door handle…</em></li>\n</ul>","a1-8x-automatic-headlight-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_auswahl-steuergerate-rls-wws-bord-c6f10e6e.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_bordnetz_rls_autobahnlicht_regenl-c0c525c9.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-automatic-headlight-activation-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong>, Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Rain Light Function Active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_auswahl-steuergerate-rls-wws-bord-c6f10e6e.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_bordnetz_rls_autobahnlicht_regenl-c0c525c9.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-aux-in-activation-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the AUX (Auxiliary) socket on the rear of the MMI 2G 3G 3GPLUS, for retrofitting to CarPlay / Android Auto / MP3 / BT box / AUX cable. You’ll also see “AUX” as an option in the multimedia menu on the central screen once you’ve completed the activation process.   </p>\n<p>When installing a CarPlay and Android Auto box kit on your MMI, you may wish to enable the AUX pin on the head unit on some cars (normally cars equipped with the Audi AMI multimedia interface). <br/>Note: if you have the Audi AMI interface, you can also use an AMI-AUX adapter instead of activating AUX. This will work fine, but you’ll need to run a cable to the AMI input. Although this works correctly, the cable is not hidden.    <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<h2><strong>For MMI 2G / 3G</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu) the tutorial is available according to your MMI model</em> <em>in the vehicle list.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Activate AUX in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + MENU</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p><strong><em>MMI 2G : </em></strong>DIAG SETTINGS -&gt; APK 0x01, -&gt; Stereo Aux In <em>(Check)</em> -&gt; accept changes <em>(to validate the modification)</em></p>\n<p><strong><em>MMI 3G :</em></strong> diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; ami_aux -&gt; Select <strong>AUX [enabled] 1/2</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_ami_bt-fdaa8044.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p><em>Press MENU + Wheel + Top Right button.</em></p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>For MMI 3G / 3GP</h2>\n<p><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte<strong>“8</strong>“<br/>Check bit<strong>“4</strong>” AUX-IN [PR-UE3] <em>to activate your MMI AUX output</em></p>\n<p><em>Uncheck AMI bit<strong>“5”</strong>[PR-UE7] if you’re using a Carplay box without an AMI adapter and you have the original AMI plug.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Activater-AUX-616c1060.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-vehicle-lock-unlock-beeps":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables beeps when locking or unlocking the vehicle.  </p>\n<p>Only for vehicles with the factory-installed alarm <br/>(1 beep to lock, 2 beeps to unlock)  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>05</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation via Horn Active”</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Unlocking Confirmation via Horn active”</em></p>\n<p>Enable the “lock tone” display in the MMI:<br/><em>Byte <strong>05</strong>: </em><br/>Set <em>Bit <strong>2</strong></em></p>","a1-8x-change-mmi-rmc-start-logo":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the Splash Screen of the MMI RMC.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>03</strong></p>\n<p><strong>standard</strong> logo:<br/>Bit <strong>0</strong> disabled<br/>Bit <strong>1</strong> disabled</p>\n<p><strong>S-Line</strong> logo:<br/>Bit <strong>0</strong> enabled<br/>Bit <strong>1</strong> disabled</p>\n<p><strong>S</strong> logo: <br/>Bit <strong>0</strong> disabled<br/>Bit <strong>1</strong> enabled</p>\n<p><strong>RS</strong> logo: <br/>Bit <strong>0</strong> enabled<br/>Bit <strong>1</strong> enabled</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6878-168e78a3.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-comfort-flashing-light":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the number of flashes for the “Comfort flashing” option.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– In the drop-down list, select<strong> Channel 31</strong><strong>“Comfort Turn Signal”.</strong> </p>\n<p>Choose a value between 1 and 5 for the number of flashes</p>","a1-8x-coming-leaving-home-with-daytime-running-lights-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows use of daytime running lights (DRL) for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  <br/><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>14</strong>: Bit <strong>0: </strong> Uncheck “Front Fog Light Installed”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG09_Bordnetz_Byte14_Ansteuerung_Comin-6c9ae70a.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-coming-leaving-home-with-fog-lamps":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Enables fog lamps to be used for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>17</strong>: Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) via Fog-Light active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5_774-e325de60.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-coming-leaving-home-with-the-xenons":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Activates xenon headlamps instead of fog lamps for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>17 </strong>:  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck “Coming-Home (CH) via Fog-Light active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG09_Bordnetz_Byte17_Ansteuerung_Comin-58ed40b4.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-corner-lights-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activating the <strong>turn signals</strong> causes the fog light on the side toward which you’re turning the steering wheel to turn on when traveling at speeds below 50 km/h. This feature is also known as “cornering lights.” Once this feature is activated on your Audi A1, the fog light on the side of the turn you’re making will turn on! It’s super handy on narrow roads or in roundabouts.     </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Control Unit</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4-Activation-des-feux-en-virage-sur-Golf-5-et-6-f4e51c90.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select  </p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>14</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7</strong>: Check “Cornering Lights via Front Fog Lights active”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG09_Bordnetz_Byte14_Ansteuerung_Comin-6c9ae70a.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – After completing this step, click on the “Exit” menu<br/>, then click “OK.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-2a08cc40.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-cruise-control-activation-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to activate GRA cruise control (retrofit). </p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible after retrofit of cruise control switch.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on “Select”. <strong><strong>01 – Engine</strong></strong> ” .<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select byte<strong>“5</strong>“<br/>Select bit<strong>“5-6</strong>” 20 Cruise Control System (CCS) installed</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/GRA01audia1q3-ab240415.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on ” <strong>16 – Multifunction steering wheel</strong> ” .<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select byte<strong>“5</strong>“<br/>Select bit<strong>“4-7</strong>” 20 Cruise Control controlled via Separate Lever</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/GRA16audia1q3-5e5972a1.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-deactivate-brake-pad-warning-light":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable the brake pad wear warning light on the OBD (On-Board Diagnostics) system, for example, for brake pads without a sensor or if the sensor is malfunctioning / Brake Pad Warning Light Deactivation. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>17 – Instruments</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “ <strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then click “ <strong>Long Coding Helper.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>: “<br/>” Then uncheck bit <strong>0: </strong> <strong>“Brakepad warning active/installed”</strong> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant-frein-d4619ec9.gif\"/></figure>","a1-8x-deactivate-windshield-washer-indicator":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the windshield washer indicator on the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>2: </strong>“<strong>Washer Fluid warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/laveglace-edc83d4f.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-defrost-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the operating time for mirror and rear window defrosting.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong> then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 25</strong> (Rear Window &amp; Outside Mirror Heater Activation Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select the desired duration</p>\n<p><em>Please note that a multiplier of <strong>40</strong> applies to the value you choose.<br/>Ex: If you choose <strong>15</strong>, the duration will be <strong>15 * 40 = 600 sec.</strong></em></p>","a1-8x-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt. <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Bit <strong>1</strong> disabled: <strong>“Seat Belt Warning active/installed”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong><em>OR</em></strong><br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Desactivate seat belt warning</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Oui</strong>” /<strong>“Yes</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/8U0_920_940_Module17_Adaptation_desactivate_seat_b-77d3b532.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-disable-start-stop-display-in-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the Start and Stop indicator in the ODB (On-Board Computer).  <br/></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17- Instruments”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong>Start/Stop indicator</strong> <strong>”</strong><br/><br/> 6 – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but towards the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, choose “<strong>Off</strong>” then validate.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6880-89412b73.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-disable-rear-wiper-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate automatic activation of the rear windshield wiper during reversing when the front windshield wipers are operating.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em><strong>Byte 21:</strong></em><br/><em><strong>Bit 6: </strong> Uncheck “Automatic Rear Window Wiping with Reverse Gear Active”</em></p>","a1-8x-deactivation-of-audi-parking-system-engagement-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: deactivates the beep when the Audi Parking System is engaged.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>10 – Assistance stationn</strong>”.  <br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select “<strong>Tonalité d’activation de l’aide au stationnement </strong>” / “<strong>Park assist activation</strong> <strong>tone </strong>” / “<strong>Aktivierungston für Einparkhilfe </strong>” from value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select<strong>“Off”</strong> in the second value list</p>","a1-8x-parking-aid-display-on-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the display of reversing radars on the MMI, for vehicles with the Audi Parking System rear option only.  </p>\n<p><strong>Requires at least module 8X0-919-475-F</strong> </p>\n<p><em>On certain vehicles equipped with the 8X0-919-475-F module, activation does not work.</em><br/><em>There are no issues with vehicles equipped with the 8X0-919-475-M module.</em> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1<strong>– </strong>Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to<br/>the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2 </strong>– Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong> and then click on “<strong>10 – Assistance stationn</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Byte<strong> 0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bits <strong>2–3</strong>: Select “08 Optical Illustration active (BAP NEW)”</em></p>\n<p>If this does not work after restarting the MMI, select “04 Active Optical Display (BAP ALT)”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG10_Einparkhilfe_Byte0_optische_Darst-f612eaaa.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Method 1</strong></p>\n<p>Hold <strong>MENU (1)</strong> + <strong>Wheel (2)</strong> + <strong>Top right button (3)</strong> for 6 sec.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/reboot_mmi_a1_q3-54f2b780.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Method 2</strong> <em>(if method 1 doesn’t work)</em></p>\n<p>Hold <strong>BACK (1)</strong> + <strong>Wheel (2)</strong> + <strong>Top Right Button (3)</strong> for 6 sec.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audia18xmmireset-bb3a9fe0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong> and then click on “<strong>10 – Assistance stationn</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Select “Visual display for park assist” from the drop-down list</em></p>\n<p><em>Change value with <strong>OPS Display</strong></em></p>","a1-8x-activate-hill-start-assist":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables Audi Hill Start Assist.  </p>\n<p><strong>Caution:</strong> Do not confuse<strong> this</strong> with<strong> Audi Hold Assist</strong>, which keeps the vehicle stationary on uphill and downhill slopes for as long as desired. If the vehicle remains stationary for an extended period, the system automatically switches to the electromechanical brake. Audi Hold Assist requires the following button (see image) to activate and deactivate it.    </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_hold_assist-e935e41b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Audi Hill Start Assist is a hill-start assist feature. If you hold down the brake pedal for a certain amount of time while the vehicle is stopped, brake pressure is maintained for a few seconds after you release the brake pedal, making it easier to start on a hill.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong><strong>Brakes </strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>” then<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>16</strong>: </em> <br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Hill Hold Control (HHC/PR-UG1/UG4) active/installed”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a3_8p_rdk_stg03_brake_anpassen-JPG-ec6bf48f.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong><strong>Brakes </strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Channel 58 Hill Hold Control</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6 – </strong> On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the value based on your preference:</p>\n<p><em>Change the value to 0, 1, or 2<br/>0: “Normal” Hill Hold Control (HHC)<br/>1: “Early” Hill Hold Control (HHC) (the vehicle starts moving with less acceleration)<br/>2: “Late” Hill Hold Control (HHC) (the vehicle starts moving with more acceleration)</em></p>\n<p>then click “Submit.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a3_8p_stg03_bremse_hillhold-JPG-6a099c48.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-correction-of-odb-consumption-display":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to correct the fuel consumption display on the onboard computer. </p>\n<p><em>Note: The changes you make affect the display of instantaneous fuel consumption, average fuel consumption, and fuel quantity.</em> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click <strong> “17 – Instruments.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the <strong>Channel:</strong> <em>“Display correction of <em>consumption and operating range</em>“</em></p>\n<p><em>Set the consumption correction factor between 85% and 115%</em> <em>(base value: 100)</em></p>\n<p><em>Example 1: Calculation based on volume per distance (e.g., l/100 km): Target: 9.3 l/100 km. Actual: 9.8 l/100 km. (100, 9.8 / 9.73 ? 105.38) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 105.<br/>Example 2: Calculation based on distance per volume (e.g., MPG): Target: 23 MPG. Actual: 24 MPG. (100, 23/24, and 95.83) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 96       </em>.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/consomqb-7270c66a.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><em>Example 3: The fuel consumption reported by the ODB is 5.9 L/100 km; after testing, it is actually 6.3 L/100 km.<br/>Calculation of the rate to be entered: (6.3 * 100) / 5.9 = 106.78. The rate used will be 107%; the fuel consumption figure reported by the ODB will be approximately 0.1 L/100 km too low. </em></p>\n<p>Consumption is immediately modified on the MMI.</p>","a1-8x-aps-radar-frequency":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to select the Audi Parking System radar frequency.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 (Rear radar frequency) :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>10 – Assistance stationn</strong>”.  <br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p>5 – Select<em>“Speaker frequency for rear park assist</em>” from the value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Choose the new value from the second list (from Stage 1 to Stage 9)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Front Radar<strong>Frequency</strong> ):</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click <strong>“10 – Parking Assist”</strong> <br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p>5 – Select<em>“Speaker frequency for front park assist</em>” from the value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Choose the new value from the second list (from Stage 1 to Stage 9)</p>","a1-8x-flash-mode-lights-during-emergency-braking":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the brake/turn signal lights in flash mode during emergency braking.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Brake Light active” (to activate brake lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Turn Signal active” (to activate turn signals)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_stg46_komfortsystem_notbremsblinken-PNG-94b80fdc.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-retrofit-led-taillights":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to adapt the taillights on the Audi A1 8X after upgrading from the halogen version to the LED version. (Retrofit)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Control Unit</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select  </p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>18</strong>: (to be edited in the hex field)</em><br/><strong>6E</strong> = halogen headlights, LED taillights <br/><strong>6F</strong> = halogen headlights, LED taillights (taillights turn on with DRL <br/><strong>72</strong> = xenon headlights, LED taillights <br/><strong>73</strong> = xenon headlights, LED taillights (taillights turn on with DRL)</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – After completing this step, click on the “Exit” menu<br/>, then click “OK.”</p>\n<h4>Hardware Upgrade:</h4>\n<p>Would you like to retrofit LED taillights on your Audi A1 8X at a later date? This means that the combined effect of the front LED daytime running lights and the activated taillights will be even better. You can easily perform the retrofit yourself or have it done by a professional:  </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pre-facelift LED taillight: <br/><br/>Left: 8X0 945 093 E <br/>Right: 8X0 945 093 E <br/><br/>2x connector: 3B0 972 724 <br/>12-pin: 000 979 131 EA if necessary</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Facelift LED Taillight: <br/><br/>Left: 8XA 945 093 A <br/>Right: 8XA 945 094 A <br/><br/>2x connector: 1J0 972 723 <br/>12-pin: 000 979 133 EA required</li>\n</ul>\n<p>New vehicle-side connectors are required for the pre-facelift and facelift models. New pins are required, however, only when converting to the facelift model; when converting to the pre-facelift LED model, the old pins are compatible. The pin assignments for the LED are as follows:  </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Left connector pinout: <br/>Pin 1: brown <br/>Pin 2: black/yellow <br/>Pin 3: green/yellow (gray/green) <br/>Pin 4: black/white <br/>Pin 5: black/blue <br/>Pin 6: gray/white</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Straight connector pinout: <br/><br/>Pin 1: brown <br/>Pin 2: black/purple <br/>Pin 3: green/yellow (gray/green) <br/>Pin 4: black/green <br/>Pin 5: black/blue <br/>Pin 6: gray/white</li>\n</ul>","a1-8x-lock-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-mmi-rmc":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks/unlocks the CD/DVD eject button on the MMI RMC.</p>\n<p><em>Protection against CD theft.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“5F – Information Electr.</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 10</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong> <em>for active eject lock.</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart the MMI RMC.</em></p>\n<p>To eject the CD/DVD, set the value to <strong>0</strong> for normal use of the button.  </p>","a1-8x-lower-passenger-mirror-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically lowers the passenger mirror when reversing.  </p>\n<p>The mirror adjustment knob must be in position<strong>“R”</strong> for the passenger mirror to lower automatically.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“52 – Passenger door</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“4</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“2</strong>”:<strong>“Reserve Gear Mirror Dipping active</strong>”<br/>and Bit<strong>“3</strong>”:<strong>“Position Memory for Reserve Gear Mirror Dipping active</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Golf-7-Abaisser-le-retroviseur-passager-lors-de-la-9710a97c.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“09 – Central Elec</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/> 5 – Choose byte<strong>“4</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Check <em>Bit <strong>3</strong> (If this is a hidden bit, you must modify the value directly in binary (replace the 0 by 1, e.g.<strong>01011100)</strong>.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/a1_boutons_vitre-6c0b0296.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-maintain-led-intensity-with-turn-signals":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Maintains the brightness of the LEDs when the turn signals are on. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select <em>Byte <strong>15</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck “Daytime Running Light (DRL) inactive with Turn Signals active”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG09_Bordnetz_Byte15_LED_TFL_beim_Blin-10ec6fb5.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-mmi-sound-reduction-with-audi-parking-system":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: automatically reduces the MMI sound when using the Audi Parking System.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>10 – Assistance stationn</strong>”.  <br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p>5 – Select<em>“Audio reduction request</em>” from the value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select<strong>“On”</strong> in the second value list</p>","a1-8x-needle-check":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> activates needle sweep when the car is started. (Needle Sweep)   <br/></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>” then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu to choose a channel and select the “<strong>Staging</strong>” channel, if unavailable select the “<strong>indicator_celebration</strong>” channel:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg6-9456b738.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the “<strong>New value</strong>” box, click on the drop-down menu and select “<strong>active</strong>”. Once this new value has been entered, click on “<strong>Save</strong>”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg62-c8918051.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-odb-efficiency-indicator-display":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the efficiency indicator to be displayed on the ODB (On Board Computer) for an efficient, environmentally-friendly driving style.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then check Bit <strong>7: </strong><strong>“Bodycomputer</strong>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/affichage-efficacite-a1-8x-886898b9.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-rear-daytime-running-lights-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the rear lights to function as daytime running lights at the same time as the front TFL LEDs (Scandinavian DRL).</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Coding – 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 18: </strong></p>\n<p>Set Bit <strong>0</strong> </p>\n<p>Halogen: 6D or binary (01101101).</p>","a1-8x-coming-home-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is locked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 23</strong> (Coming-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG09_Bordnetz_Anpassung_Coming-Home-Ti-1e5039c6.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-leaving-home-duration-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is unlocked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 24</strong> (Leaving-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG09_Bordnetz_Anpassung_Leaving-Home-T-f7eb1bf9.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-start-stop-deactivation":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to disable Start and Stop completely.  <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“26</strong>”<br/>Then uncheck Bit<strong>“0”</strong>.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong> “Indicateur pour fonctionnement start-stop”</strong> /<strong>“Control lamp for start-stop operation</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“Deactivate</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6880-89412b73.webp\"/></figure>","a1-8x-activate-deactivate-daytime-running-lights-drl-from-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate/deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) from the MMI.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then <strong>“<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte <strong>15</strong>: <br/>Bit<strong> 7</strong>: This is a hidden bit, so modify the value directly in binary (replace 0 with 1).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG09_Bordnetz_Byte15_LED_TFL_beim_Blin-b9e04d81.webp\"/></figure>\n<h3><strong><em>MMI operation</em></strong></h3>\n<p>Menu CAR -&gt; Vehicle settings -&gt; Exterior lighting</p>\n<p>The “Daytime Running Lights” menu has been added (activation/deactivation with On/Off).</p>","a1-8x-daytime-running-light-deactivation-drl-with-handbrake":"<p> <strong>Purpose: </strong>to deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) when the handbrake is engaged.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/>Bit <strong>0</strong>: If this is a hidden bit, you must modify the binary value directly (replace the 0 with a 1)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_A1_8X_STG09_Bordnetz_Byte11_LED_TFL_inaktiv_b-d4fbba04.webp\"/></figure>"};
